//! The `PRE`-family prerequisite tokens the book archetype-swap master rows
//! carry, relocated off the live side — SD-35 `AT-35-E6-003-SWEEP` cycle 2,
//! enforcing `decisions.md` §11 (nothing on the live side reads a PCGen
//! token).
//!
//! # Why these moved, and why they were not deleted
//!
//! `rules_tables::archetype_swap::ArchetypeSwapEntry` carried a
//! `prerequisites: Option<&'static [&'static str]>` field holding every
//! top-level `PRE`-family token of the archetype's master row, verbatim.
//! **Nothing read it** — not `archetype_resolver`, which states in its own
//! module doc that evaluating an archetype's prerequisites "is
//! `feat_prereqs`' job elsewhere", and not `feat_prereqs`, which reads the
//! CONVERTED `Applies` gate out of `data/sheet_rules/` and never a token
//! string. Re-derive the absence:
//!
//! ```text
//! grep -rn "prerequisites" src apps/desktop/src-tauri/src --include=*.rs \
//!   | grep -v "rules_tables/" | grep -v failing_prerequisites
//! ```
//!
//! So this is a **move, not a removal** (`decisions.md` §11: the converter
//! side is KEPT and reused for Starfinder). The tokens are the provenance of
//! each converted archetype gate — `AGENTS.md` rule 9 — and they now live on
//! the side that owns the ingest format. Restoring the 409 rows to any
//! consumer is a keyed lookup away; nothing was lost, and no function body
//! was deleted.
//!
//! Keyed by the master row's own corpus `KEY:`, in each book's own source
//! order, exactly as the live tables held them. A row is absent when the
//! corpus record carried no `PRE`-family token at all — the same
//! `None`-when-absent rule the removed field documented.

